00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.610
How many times will it take until you get it?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.400
The idea of a disease that turns 
people into murderers is absurd!

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:42.450
The government is using that as an excuse 
because they can't figure out what's going on!

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:44.400
It's their idea of damage control!

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.800
It's Japan's favorite way of pretending to care!

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.770
So what? You're saying that 
dead bodies really are moving around?{"are really" to "really are" -A0}

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:51.930
Ridiculous!

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:55.590
It seems like some new disease! It has to be!

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:58.710
Indeed! There must be a reason for all of this!

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.110
You can think whatever you'd like,

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.560
but there's no way that amateurs could figure out the reason.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.860
It's futile unless you happen to be a specialist

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.750
with a steady environment 
and a lot of time to investigate!

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.940
There's no way any of us could do that!

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.030
Or are you trying to say that you're capable of that?

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.700
Er, that's...

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.150
You can't, can you?

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.810
You just need to get by without getting eaten!

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.410
There's nothing more important than that!

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.910
Isn't that what my dad said?

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.940
Oh, I see. That's all you wanted to say, isn't it?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:38.260
I was wondering why bratty high-schoolers were walking around with guns.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.450
Huh?

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.970
So that's what this is about!

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.990
This protection you're offering is just talk!

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:48.390
The people at this mansion are 
trying to control us through force!

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.810
Our world has become this violent

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.110
and it's a problem for people all over Asia!
How could you do this?!

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:56.180
Why are you bringing up the rest of Asia?

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.060
Listen up, everyone!

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.690
That man telling us to kill people—

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.780
No, this is the daughter

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.150
of that man who is coercing us into thinking that killing is acceptable!

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:09.560
Uhm, what are you trying to say?

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.690
This isn't something that children should be butting in on!

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.300
Children?

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.830
What do you know about the things we've—

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.400
Nonsense! We adults are going to call the shots now!

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.700
Peace loving adults, that is! 
Not the filthy pigs of the upper class

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.340
or high-schoolers drunk on violence!

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.190
Yeah!

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:32.100
We're against using force to control people!

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:33.740
Against!

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.270
Takagi-san, y-you did well.{"You did w-well, Takagi-san" to "Takagi-san., y-you did well." -A0}

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:40.600
That sucked.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:44.800
I wanted to give her a piece of my mind since
she spoke ill of my dad, but it was pointless.{"
 since she spoke ill of my dad, but it went nowhere" to "since
 she spoke ill of my dad, but it was pointless." -A0}

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.200
Have those guys seriously not seen anything?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.280
They probably shut their eyes!

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.710
I kind of understand how they feel though.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.130
You wanna fight about it, fatass?

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.350
N-No! Not at all.{added "Not at all" -too much speach for "no" -A0}

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.890
Humans don't see what they don't want to see.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.800
No one wants to be put down.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:17.430
That's why people do nothing,
 even when they do know something is happening.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:21.980
But now isn't the time to pretend that nothing has changed.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.250
Yeah... But right now,

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:30.290
the first thing people want to do is
 make things go back to how they used to be.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:31.850
No matter what.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:36.110
During times when they know from the start
 that it isn't going to work out,

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.290
if they ask themselves why—

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.780
If they don't acknowledge something has changed,

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.870
they don't have to acknowledge their own faults and stupidity.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.070
Y-Yeah.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:50.780
I thought about what happened at school and stuff,
 then came to that realization...

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:54.150
My opinion of you went up a little.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:55.540
So that's it.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:56.220
What is?

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.000
I learned something.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:04.290
What?

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:06.370
When you say that...

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.610
Huh? I know it's embarrassing, 
but at least I'm acknowledging it!

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.220
Eh? Don't you think it should be him?

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.460
Yup! Sure does seem that way!

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.090
What're you guys talking about?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.520
Did you forget?

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:24.020
This is why you're capable of being our leader!

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.450
...huh?

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.620
What does that look like?

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:48.180
I've heard that Busujima-sensei's daughter is a swordswoman on par with Chiba Sanako.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:54.440
You must be a pure and graceful Japanese maiden.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.580
Touching the sword directly will not taint it.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:04.480
This is...

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.700
How very unusual.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:10.960
Do you see now?

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.430
It has a shallow curve on the hamon.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:17.330
That indicates this double-edge tipped blade is a
Kissaki Moroha Kogarasu Zuraki{Italics removed and name researched -A0}

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.140
Kanemasa Firearms.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.480
This appears to be a Murata blade, but...

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.850
You live up to my expectations.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:28.370
In the middle of the Meiji era,

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.700
Major General Murata, who was known for the Murata Rifle,

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:35.170
had that blade manufactured in the Tokyo Artillery Arsenal.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:41.520
Legend goes that he split a pig's skull{gg: "the bone of a pig's head"} in half without scratching the blade. {W.E. Original line was redundant.}

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.900
It was an honor to have seen it.{"A sight for sore eyes." seems rather crass. I took line from the manga -A0}

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.180
It belongs to you now.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:53.300
I do not mean to be rude,

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:56.410
but I cannot accept this without a proper reason.{A0}

00:07:57.140 --> 00:08:00.010
I received instruction from Busujima-sensei.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:04.660
Will you not take it as a token of my appreciation?

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.580
In that case, I shall pass it to my father.{This whole "proper and respectful" dialgue was localized a bit too much. Altered mainly using the manga -A0}

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.720
You truly are a daughter of the Busujima family.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.210
You are not subtle.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.020
Forgive me for that.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.280
As you have probably already guessed,

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.660
I am giving you this because of my own foolish daughter.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.510
Indeed, I did save her life,

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.830
however she assisted me in avoiding dangers also.{A0}

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:38.700
If you wish to go to such extremes to protect her,

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:42.350
why not keep her by your side at all times?

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:44.770
The honorable daughter of the Takagi family

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.650
holds her parents in high esteem and loves them very much.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.940
As they say, "like parent like child."

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.280
Then that is all the more reason to.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:58.420
Alternatively, you could give it to Takash— Komuro-kun, not me.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.570
He is our—

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.860
I have known of him since his youth.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:05.190
He has turned into a fine young man.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.610
That is obvious from how much you trust him.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:11.340
However...

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.010
It seems as though his heart still wavers.

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:22.940
He who leads during a crisis should...

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.900
They call me the leader, but...

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.640
But aren't you?

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.760
You okay, Rei?

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:41.170
Don't stress yourself or you'll get worse.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:44.620
We've been relying on you.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:49.260
You were brave at school and elsewhere.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:53.200
That was out of desperation. I've got nothing.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:59.960
The ones who are good at fighting are Saeko-san and Hirano. You too.{"Saeko-san and Hirano are good at fighting" to "The ones who are good at fighting are Saeko-san and Hirano" for flow -A0}

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.380
Moving along, Saya has high intelligence.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.890
Shizuka-sensei is kind of a healer.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:07.450
And Alice-chan is...

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:09.290
Alice-chan is?

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:11.290
Alice-chan is...

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:13.710
Alice-chan is Alice!

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:17.410
Hey, don't laugh.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:24.550
Takashi...

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:25.730
Yeah?

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:29.350
Let me tell you a rule that us girls have.

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:39.120
The guys who we like are cute and treat us good.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:40.860
...that's it?

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:43.220
Yup. That's it.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:45.920
What could be more important?

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:48.770
And I don't fall under either category?

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.860
You probably didn't. I'll admit that.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.330
But it's different now.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.860
Sometimes you sound so hopeless, other times you appear to be brave.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.570
You don't need a reason.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.340
You know what you have to do.

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.320
You just know, Takashi.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.150
You've always been like that.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.140
I just didn't notice.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.330
I probably didn't notice before everything began.

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:20.680
More than likely...

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.540
But that's why I want to be with you!

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.350
I'll do whatever it takes to be with you!

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:34.310
Even if you fall in love with another girl!

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:36.530
Because I won't survive if I'm not with you!

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:45.460
What's wrong?

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:51.220
I don't know if I should be happy or angry.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.610
That reasoning is too complex for my liking.{"tender" to "complex" for flow -A0}

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:02.130
Well, aren't women themselves complex?{"tender" to "complex" for consistancy -A0}

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.610
Sorry. It probably hurts. You should lie down...

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:22.330
I'll ask Sensei to look at it.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:31.420
Think carefully about the meaning of what I said.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:38.610
I sensed that someone was already inside, so I decided to wait.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.050
I did not hear any voices.

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:48.780
Sempai, you should talk to Takashi. That would make him happy.{Italics removed -A0}

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:51.350
Acknowledged.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:53.630
By the way...

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.080
Yes?

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:58.980
Would you quit referring to me as Sempai?{Italics removed -A0}

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:00.710
In reality, we are the same—

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:01.840
Don't say that.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:05.470
I don't wanna think about it.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.360
Survivors?

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:27.770
Please!

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:29.810
Please, help us!

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:35.040
We came here after we escaped from our school,
 but we have nowhere to go!

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.830
Please! Please help us!

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:40.890
Okay.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:44.160
We'll move the blockade right away.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.000
So you'll find your parents, no matter what?

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:53.770
I will.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:57.010
My father is somewhere far away, so I'll simply pray for his safety.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.660
My mother should be at 
the grade school she works,{A0}

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.880
since the outbreak happened during school hours.{A0}

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:04.730
Rei's...

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.300
...I mean, Miyamoto's father is a police officer,

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:10.180
so we should be able to find out something once we get to the East Police Station.{A0}

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.840
Her mother should be hiding at her house.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.330
What will you do once you find them?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.640
We'll leave in two days, first thing in the morning.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:26.220
It's far too dangerous to stay here right now.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:30.260
We'll find everyone and bring them here before you leave.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.630
I won't be able to look after so many people.

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:39.620
Well, if our parents need our help,
 then we'll stay with them.{A0}

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.710
If we don't come back in two days, please assume we aren't coming.{If you don't hear from me in a month, SEND LINK!}

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:50.810
I'd like you to take me with you as well.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.470
What should I say...

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.420
Are you always trying to seduce people?

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:01.830
So you don't even realize it.

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:07.520
Sa-Saeko-san, you look really good,
 but do you have enough time to get ready?

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:11.260
I think I'll be able to help.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.430
Besides, if you're going to bring your parents back,

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:17.380
you need enough people to guide them.

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:20.170
Well, yeah, but...

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:21.080
Rei!

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:25.290
What's wrong?

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:27.370
That's...

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:32.610
I never thought we would end up saving a member of Senator Shidou's family.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:37.070
Though this isn't exactly a time to worry about the election.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.360
It's not a problem.

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.510
I'm nothing more than a teacher at the moment.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.730
You're quite impressive.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:49.940
I heard you escaped from school with the students who survived.

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:51.860
It isn't anything special.

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:53.340
I simply fulfilled my duty as a teacher.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:55.400
Of course.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.670
Your father raised you well.

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:03.110
<i>Raised me well? Yeah, right.{Italics added -A0}</i>

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.290
My father was a senator.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:12.660
<i>But to me, he was nothing more than a selfish man.{Italics added -A0}</i>

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:16.550
{Italics added -A0}He abandoned my mother,
 who ultimately committed suicide.{Italics added -A0}

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:21.110
{Italics added -A0}I left my home to become a teacher, but...{Italics added -A0}

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:26.930
There's this one annoying guy from the security police.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:30.540
His daughter goes to your school.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.690
Make her flunk a grade.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.410
That should teach him a lesson or two.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.750
Can you at least save the students?

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:44.550
I'll manage on my—

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:49.300
My, you're so admirable, Shidou-sensei.

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:52.360
Mi-Miyamoto-san.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.340
I'm glad you're safe.

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:58.660
Do you know why I'm good with the spear?

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:01.380
It's because I learned how to use a bayonet. {"Because I also know how to use a rifle sword."to "It's because I learned how to use a bayonet" -for clarity -A0}

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:04.510
My father, the best in the
prefecture police, taught me.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.940
And you made my father suffer.

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:11.590
He never yielded to anything,
 but he apologized to me in tears!

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:15.690
He shouldered the blame for me being held back a year.{"That he made me flunk a grade." -for flow -A0}

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.320
And I know!

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:22.030
I know that you're the only one 
who could do that to my grades!

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.390
But I held myself down.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:30.580
Because he told me that he could arrest both you and Senator Shidou if his investigation went well.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:31.630
But now...

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.760
A-Are you going to kill me?

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:42.470
You're going to become a criminal,
 even though your father is a police officer?!

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:44.540
You're one to talk!

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:46.560
Then kill him!

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:53.720
I'm somewhat acquainted with his father,

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.820
but in this age and time, that's useless.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:00.000
If you wish for it, then kill him!

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:02.730
S-Saeko-san!

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:06.870
Miyamoto-kun must decide this for herself.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.220
Very well.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:10.740
Kill me.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:16.320
Kill me and suffer for it as long as you live!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:20.940
That is the highest level of education

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:22.570
I can give you

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.040
as your teacher!

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.940
Is that your decision?

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.270
He's not even worth my time.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:03.140
Take your leave!

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.700
You've already been tainted with his stupidity.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.790
Leave with your students!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:26.050
Captain, I've received a new emergency order.

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:28.100
Code 666 Delta.

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:31.180
I repeat, code 666 Delta.

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:35.980
They're orders regarding targets November-Kilo and Romeo-Charlie.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:37.020
Roger.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.430
Number One, get to the authentication station!{001, get to the announcement station! -A0}

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:40.990
Confirm the message.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:47.540
Has the order been confirmed, Number One?{"001" -A0}

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:53.660
This is your captain.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.770
The President's order has been confirmed.

00:19:57.560 --> 00:20:03.230
We will now commence fire on November-Kilo and Romeo-Charlie!

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:09.300
Who's The President right now, anyway?

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:10.730
They all turned into monsters...

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:14.130
Is it someone from the DOE?

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:17.460
Two days ago, it was someone from the DHS.

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:19.700
Though he was already bitten.

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:20.580
Those fuckers.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:24.570
But no one knows the exact details...

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.450
Only Heaven, the angels, and ourselves.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.990
God, please forgive us.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.460
God, please save us.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:38.900
Fire 01!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.930
Hey you two, we've done so far living with burdens

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:17.600
It crawls with desires down to the earth

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:23.930
A shadow to cover my curse, only fate

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:30.460
Like dead mob rising to the feet on the ground

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:36.930
And then I feel it for the same old yesterday

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:42.210
The uncertainty of tomorrow got shatter

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:46.690
Being with you again, and shut your heart away

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:52.060
Go faster before a memory go away

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:58.970
In this world, it's over too, fall into ruin

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:05.260
Dead and too vain, we don't across, out of any where

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:10.160
Gonna keep on fighting, don't know what it is for

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:18.000
Having a fear, shall be a tear, I just keep myself together

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:32.590
Another one.{"Not yet." makes no sense -A0)

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:35.330
Not only America, but Russia is firing.

00:22:36.130 --> 00:22:37.160
Russia?

00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:39.140
They have time to fire missiles?

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:41.500
Yeah, they're following suit.

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:43.060
And these are MIRVs!

00:22:43.620 --> 00:22:47.050
There aren't many, but there's definitely enough to annihilate capitals and military bases.

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:52.710
This?!

00:22:52.810 --> 00:22:55.140
Yeah, this is the current situation.

00:23:02.550 --> 00:23:05.160
Living Dead and now First Strike? {"First strike happens after the living dead." -for flow -A0}

00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:08.220
They'd never use a plot like this in Hollywood.

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:10.410
No, it looks like they did.

00:23:12.840 --> 00:23:13.520
O God!

00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:23.330
It's Armageddon.

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:28.150
Electromagnetic pulse?

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:30.530
An EMP attack. We can't use electronics.

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:32.530
This is the Alamo!

00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:33.920
Hirano-kun, I leave my daughter in your hands.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:36.110
After today, the nights will be truly dark.
